---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ListLocationsResponse
---@field locations? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.LocationList The locations.
---@field totalSize? number The approximate number of Locations in the list irrespective of pagination. This field will only be returned if `filter` is used as a query parameter.
---@field nextPageToken? string If the number of locations exceeded the requested page size, this field is populated with a token to fetch the next page of locations on a subsequent call to `ListLocations`. If there are no more locations, this field is not present in the response.

---A location. See the [help center article] (https://support.google.com/business/answer/3038177) for a detailed description of these fields, or the [category endpoint](/my-business/reference/rest/v4/categories) for a list of valid business categories.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Location
---@field name? string Identifier. Google identifier for this location in the form: `locations/{location_id}`.
---@field phoneNumbers? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.PhoneNumbers Optional. The different phone numbers that customers can use to get in touch with the business.
---@field relationshipData? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RelationshipData Optional. All locations and chain related to this one.
---@field categories? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Categories Optional. The different categories that describe the business.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Metadata Output only. Additional non-user-editable information.
---@field regularHours? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.BusinessHours Optional. Operating hours for the business.
---@field openInfo? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.OpenInfo Optional. A flag that indicates whether the location is currently open for business.
---@field storeCode? string Optional. External identifier for this location, which must be unique within a given account. This is a means of associating the location with your own records.
---@field profile? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Profile Optional. Describes your business in your own voice and shares with users the unique story of your business and offerings. This field is required for all categories except lodging categories (e.g., hotels, motels, inns).
---@field serviceItems? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceItemList Optional. List of services supported by merchants. A service can be haircut, install water heater, etc. Duplicated service items will be removed automatically.
---@field adWordsLocationExtensions? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.AdWordsLocationExtensions Optional. Additional information that is surfaced in AdWords.
---@field languageCode? string Immutable. The language of the location. Set during creation and not updateable.
---@field websiteUri? string Optional. A URL for this business. If possible, use a URL that represents this individual business location instead of a generic website/URL that represents all locations, or the brand.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.StringList Optional. A collection of free-form strings to allow you to tag your business. These labels are NOT user facing; only you can see them. Must be between 1-255 characters per label.
---@field specialHours? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SpecialHours Optional. Special hours for the business. This typically includes holiday hours, and other times outside of regular operating hours. These override regular business hours. This field cannot be set without regular hours.
---@field title? string Required. Location name should reflect your business's real-world name, as used consistently on your storefront, website, and stationery, and as known to customers. Any additional information, when relevant, can be included in other fields of the resource (for example, `Address`, `Categories`). Don't add unnecessary information to your name (for example, prefer "Google" over "Google Inc. - Mountain View Corporate Headquarters"). Don't include marketing taglines, store codes, special characters, hours or closed/open status, phone numbers, website URLs, service/product information, location/address or directions, or containment information (for example, "Chase ATM in Duane Reade").
---@field moreHours? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.MoreHoursList Optional. More hours for a business's different departments or specific customers.
---@field serviceArea? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceAreaBusiness Optional. Service area businesses provide their service at the customer's location. If this business is a service area business, this field describes the area(s) serviced by the business.
---@field latlng? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.LatLng Optional. User-provided latitude and longitude. When creating a location, this field is ignored if the provided address geocodes successfully. This field is only returned on get requests if the user-provided `latlng` value was accepted during create, or the `latlng` value was updated through the Google Business Profile website. This field can only be updated by approved clients.
---@field storefrontAddress? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.PostalAddress Optional. A precise, accurate address to describe your business location. PO boxes or mailboxes located at remote locations are not acceptable. At this time, you can specify a maximum of five `address_lines` values in the address. This field should only be set for businesses that have a storefront. This field should not be set for locations of type `CUSTOMER_LOCATION_ONLY` but if set, any value provided will be discarded.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.LocationList gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Location[]

---Additional non-user-editable information about the location.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Metadata
---@field canModifyServiceList? boolean Output only. Indicates if the listing can modify the service list.
---@field newReviewUri? string Output only. A link to the page on Google Search where a customer can leave a review for the location.
---@field isParticularlyPersonalPlace? boolean Output only. Indicates whether the location is classified as a particularly personal place. This means there are restrictions on Location History features. If you believe this was a mistake, see the [help center article](https://support.google.com/business/answer/3480441).
---@field placeId? string Output only. If this location appears on Google Maps, this field is populated with the place ID for the location. This ID can be used in various Places APIs. This field can be set during Create calls, but not for Update.
---@field hasPendingEdits? boolean Output only. Indicates whether any of this Location's properties are in the edit pending state.
---@field canOperateLodgingData? boolean Output only. Indicates whether the location can operate on Lodging data.
---@field canDelete? boolean Output only. Indicates whether the location can be deleted using the API.
---@field canHaveFoodMenus? boolean Output only. Indicates if the listing is eligible for food menu.
---@field mapsUri? string Output only. A link to the location on Maps.
---@field canOperateLocalPost? boolean Output only. Deprecated: This field is no longer populated and will be removed in a future version.
---@field hasVoiceOfMerchant? boolean Output only. Indicates if the listing has Voice of Merchant. If this boolean is false, you should call the locations.getVoiceOfMerchantState API to get details as to why they do not have Voice of Merchant.
---@field canHaveBusinessCalls? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Relates to the Call Tracking feature which is no longer supported. Indicates whether the location is eligible for business calls.
---@field hasGoogleUpdated? boolean Output only. Indicates whether the place ID associated with this location has updates that need to be updated or rejected by the client. If this boolean is set, you should call the `getGoogleUpdated` method to look up information that's needs to be verified.
---@field canOperateHealthData? boolean Output only. Indicates whether the location can operate on Health data.
---@field duplicateLocation? string Output only. The location resource that this location duplicates.

---Represents an amount of money with its currency type.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Money
---@field nanos? number Number of nano (10^-9) units of the amount. The value must be between -999,999,999 and +999,999,999 inclusive. If `units` is positive, `nanos` must be positive or zero. If `units` is zero, `nanos` can be positive, zero, or negative. If `units` is negative, `nanos` must be negative or zero. For example $-1.75 is represented as `units`=-1 and `nanos`=-750,000,000.
---@field units? string The whole units of the amount. For example if `currencyCode` is `"USD"`, then 1 unit is one US dollar.
---@field currencyCode? string The three-letter currency code defined in ISO 4217.

---The time periods during which a location is open for certain types of business.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.MoreHours
---@field hoursTypeId? string Required. Type of hours. Clients should call {#link businessCategories:BatchGet} to get supported hours types for categories of their locations.
---@field periods? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimePeriodList Required. A collection of times that this location is open. Each period represents a range of hours when the location is open during the week.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.MoreHoursList gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.MoreHours[]

---More hours types that a business can offers, in addition to its regular hours.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.MoreHoursType
---@field hoursTypeId? string Output only. A stable ID provided by Google for this hours type.
---@field displayName? string Output only. The human-readable English display name for the hours type.
---@field localizedDisplayName? string Output only. The human-readable localized display name for the hours type.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.MoreHoursTypeList gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.MoreHoursType[]

---Represents a whole or partial calendar date, such as a birthday. The time of day and time zone are either specified elsewhere or are insignificant. The date is relative to the Gregorian Calendar. This can represent one of the following: * A full date, with non-zero year, month, and day values. * A month and day, with a zero year (for example, an anniversary). * A year on its own, with a zero month and a zero day. * A year and month, with a zero day (for example, a credit card expiration date). Related types: * google.type.TimeOfDay * google.type.DateTime * google.protobuf.Timestamp
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Mybusinessbusinessinformation_Date
---@field year? number Year of the date. Must be from 1 to 9999, or 0 to specify a date without a year.
---@field day? number Day of a month. Must be from 1 to 31 and valid for the year and month, or 0 to specify a year by itself or a year and month where the day isn't significant.
---@field month? number Month of a year. Must be from 1 to 12, or 0 to specify a year without a month and day.

---Information related to the opening state of the business.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.OpenInfo
---@field openingDate? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Mybusinessbusinessinformation_Date Optional. The date on which the location first opened. If the exact day is not known, month and year only can be provided. The date must be in the past or be no more than one year in the future.
---@field canReopen? boolean Output only. Indicates whether this business is eligible for re-open.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.OpenInfoStatusEnum|string Required. Indicates whether or not the Location is currently open for business. All locations are open by default, unless updated to be closed.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.OpenInfoStatusEnum "OPEN_FOR_BUSINESS_UNSPECIFIED"|"OPEN"|"CLOSED_PERMANENTLY"|"CLOSED_TEMPORARILY"

