---A collection of phone numbers for the business. During updates, both fields must be set. Clients may not update just the primary or additional phone numbers using the update mask. International phone format is preferred, such as "+1 415 555 0132", see more in (https://developers.google.com/style/phone-numbers#international-phone-numbers).
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.PhoneNumbers
---@field additionalPhones? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.StringList Optional. Up to two phone numbers (mobile or landline, no fax) at which your business can be called, in addition to your primary phone number.
---@field primaryPhone? string Required. A phone number that connects to your individual business location as directly as possible. Use a local phone number instead of a central, call center helpline number whenever possible.

---Defines an area that's represented by a place ID.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.PlaceInfo
---@field placeId? string Required. The ID of the place. Must correspond to a region. (https://developers.google.com/places/web-service/supported_types#table3)
---@field placeName? string Required. The localized name of the place. For example, `Scottsdale, AZ`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.PlaceInfoList gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.PlaceInfo[]

---Defines the union of areas represented by a set of places.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Places
---@field placeInfos? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.PlaceInfoList Optional. The areas represented by place IDs. Limited to a maximum of 20 places.

---Represents a postal address, such as for postal delivery or payments addresses. With a postal address, a postal service can deliver items to a premise, P.O. box, or similar. A postal address is not intended to model geographical locations like roads, towns, or mountains. In typical usage, an address would be created by user input or from importing existing data, depending on the type of process. Advice on address input or editing: - Use an internationalization-ready address widget such as https://github.com/google/libaddressinput. - Users should not be presented with UI elements for input or editing of fields outside countries where that field is used. For more guidance on how to use this schema, see: https://support.google.com/business/answer/6397478.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.PostalAddress
---@field locality? string Optional. Generally refers to the city or town portion of the address. Examples: US city, IT comune, UK post town. In regions of the world where localities are not well defined or do not fit into this structure well, leave `locality` empty and use `address_lines`.
---@field sortingCode? string Optional. Additional, country-specific, sorting code. This is not used in most regions. Where it is used, the value is either a string like "CEDEX", optionally followed by a number (for example, "CEDEX 7"), or just a number alone, representing the "sector code" (Jamaica), "delivery area indicator" (Malawi) or "post office indicator" (Côte d'Ivoire).
---@field sublocality? string Optional. Sublocality of the address. For example, this can be a neighborhood, borough, or district.
---@field postalCode? string Optional. Postal code of the address. Not all countries use or require postal codes to be present, but where they are used, they may trigger additional validation with other parts of the address (for example, state or zip code validation in the United States).
---@field languageCode? string Optional. BCP-47 language code of the contents of this address (if known). This is often the UI language of the input form or is expected to match one of the languages used in the address' country/region, or their transliterated equivalents. This can affect formatting in certain countries, but is not critical to the correctness of the data and will never affect any validation or other non-formatting related operations. If this value is not known, it should be omitted (rather than specifying a possibly incorrect default). Examples: "zh-Hant", "ja", "ja-Latn", "en".
---@field addressLines? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.StringList Unstructured address lines describing the lower levels of an address. Because values in `address_lines` do not have type information and may sometimes contain multiple values in a single field (for example, "Austin, TX"), it is important that the line order is clear. The order of address lines should be "envelope order" for the country or region of the address. In places where this can vary (for example, Japan), `address_language` is used to make it explicit (for example, "ja" for large-to-small ordering and "ja-Latn" or "en" for small-to-large). In this way, the most specific line of an address can be selected based on the language. The minimum permitted structural representation of an address consists of a `region_code` with all remaining information placed in the `address_lines`. It would be possible to format such an address very approximately without geocoding, but no semantic reasoning could be made about any of the address components until it was at least partially resolved. Creating an address only containing a `region_code` and `address_lines` and then geocoding is the recommended way to handle completely unstructured addresses (as opposed to guessing which parts of the address should be localities or administrative areas).
---@field regionCode? string Required. CLDR region code of the country/region of the address. This is never inferred and it is up to the user to ensure the value is correct. See https://cldr.unicode.org/ and https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/30/supplemental/territory_information.html for details. Example: "CH" for Switzerland.
---@field administrativeArea? string Optional. Highest administrative subdivision which is used for postal addresses of a country or region. For example, this can be a state, a province, an oblast, or a prefecture. For Spain, this is the province and not the autonomous community (for example, "Barcelona" and not "Catalonia"). Many countries don't use an administrative area in postal addresses. For example, in Switzerland, this should be left unpopulated.
---@field organization? string Optional. The name of the organization at the address.
---@field revision? number The schema revision of the `PostalAddress`. This must be set to 0, which is the latest revision. All new revisions **must** be backward compatible with old revisions.
---@field recipients? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.StringList Optional. The recipient at the address. This field may, under certain circumstances, contain multiline information. For example, it might contain "care of" information.

---All information pertaining to the location's profile.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Profile
---@field description? string Required. Description of the location in your own voice, not editable by anyone else.

---Information of all parent and children locations related to this one.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RelationshipData
---@field childrenLocations? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RelevantLocationList Optional. The list of children locations that this location has relations with.
---@field parentLocation? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RelevantLocation Optional. The parent location that this location has relations with.
---@field parentChain? string Optional. The resource name of the Chain that this location is member of. How to find Chain ID

---Information about another location that is related to current one. The relation can be any one of DEPARTMENT_OF or INDEPENDENT_ESTABLISHMENT_OF, and the location specified here can be on either side (parent/child) of the location.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RelevantLocation
---@field placeId? string Required. Specify the location that is on the other side of the relation by its placeID.
---@field relationType? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RelevantLocationRelationTypeEnum|string Required. The type of the relationship.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RelevantLocationList gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RelevantLocation[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RelevantLocationRelationTypeEnum "RELATION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DEPARTMENT_OF"|"INDEPENDENT_ESTABLISHMENT_IN"

---Values for an attribute with a `value_type` of REPEATED_ENUM. This consists of two lists of value IDs: those that are set (true) and those that are unset (false). Values absent are considered unknown. At least one value must be specified.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.RepeatedEnumAttributeValue
---@field unsetValues? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.StringList Enum values that are unset.
---@field setValues? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.StringList Enum values that are set.

---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SearchChainsRequest
---@field chainName? string Required. Search for a chain by its name. Exact/partial/fuzzy/related queries are supported. Examples: "walmart", "wal-mart", "walmmmart", "沃尔玛"
---@field pageSize? number The maximum number of matched chains to return from this query. The default is 10. The maximum possible value is 500.

---Response message for Locations.SearchChains.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SearchChainsResponse
---@field chains? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ChainList Chains that match the queried chain_display_name in SearchChainsRequest. If there are no matches, this field will be empty. Results are listed in order of relevance.

---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SearchGoogleLocationsRequest_
---@field location? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Location Location to search for. If provided, will find locations which match the provided location details, which must include a value for the title.
---@field pageSize? number The number of matches to return. The default value is 3, with a maximum of 10. Note that latency may increase if more are requested. There is no pagination.
---@field query? string Text query to search for. The search results from a query string will be less accurate than if providing an exact location, but can provide more inexact matches.

---Response message for GoogleLocations.SearchGoogleLocations.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SearchGoogleLocationsResponse
---@field googleLocations? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.GoogleLocationList A collection of GoogleLocations that are potential matches to the specified request, listed in order from most to least accuracy.

---Service area businesses provide their service at the customer's location (for example, a locksmith or plumber).
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceAreaBusiness
---@field regionCode? string Immutable. CLDR region code of the country/region that this service area business is based in. See http://cldr.unicode.org/ and http://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/30/supplemental/territory_information.html for details. Example: "CH" for Switzerland. This field is required for CUSTOMER_LOCATION_ONLY businesses, and is ignored otherwise. The region specified here can be different from regions for the areas that this business serves (e.g. service area businesses that provide services in regions other than the one that they are based in). If this location requires verification after creation, the address provided for verification purposes *must* be located within this region, and the business owner or their authorized representative *must* be able to receive postal mail at the provided verification address.
---@field places? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Places Optional. The area that this business serves defined through a set of places.
---@field businessType? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceAreaBusinessBusinessTypeEnum|string Required. Indicates the type of the service area business.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceAreaBusinessBusinessTypeEnum "BUSINESS_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CUSTOMER_LOCATION_ONLY"|"CUSTOMER_AND_BUSINESS_LOCATION"

---A message that describes a single service item. It is used to describe the type of service that the merchant provides. For example, haircut can be a service.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceItem
---@field structuredServiceItem? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.StructuredServiceItem Optional. This field will be set case of structured services data.
---@field price? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Money Optional. Represents the monetary price of the service item. We recommend that currency_code and units should be set when including a price. This will be treated as a fixed price for the service item.
---@field freeFormServiceItem? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.FreeFormServiceItem Optional. This field will be set case of free-form services data.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceItemList gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceItem[]

---A message describing a service type that the business offers.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceType
---@field serviceTypeId? string Output only. A stable ID (provided by Google) for this service type.
---@field displayName? string Output only. The human-readable display name for the service type.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceTypeList gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.ServiceType[]

---Represents a single time period when a location's operational hours differ from its normal business hours. A special hour period must represent a range of less than 24 hours. The `open_time` and `start_date` must predate the `close_time` and `end_date`. The `close_time` and `end_date` can extend to 11:59 a.m. on the day after the specified `start_date`. For example, the following inputs are valid: start_date=2015-11-23, open_time=08:00, close_time=18:00 start_date=2015-11-23, end_date=2015-11-23, open_time=08:00, close_time=18:00 start_date=2015-11-23, end_date=2015-11-24, open_time=13:00, close_time=11:59 The following inputs are not valid: start_date=2015-11-23, open_time=13:00, close_time=11:59 start_date=2015-11-23, end_date=2015-11-24, open_time=13:00, close_time=12:00 start_date=2015-11-23, end_date=2015-11-25, open_time=08:00, close_time=18:00
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SpecialHourPeriod
---@field openTime? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimeOfDay Optional. Valid values are 00:00-24:00 where 24:00 represents midnight at the end of the specified day field. Must be specified if `closed` is false.
---@field endDate? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Mybusinessbusinessinformation_Date Optional. The calendar date this special hour period ends on. If `end_date` field is not set, default to the date specified in `start_date`. If set, this field must be equal to or at most 1 day after `start_date`.
---@field closed? boolean Optional. If true, `end_date`, `open_time`, and `close_time` are ignored, and the date specified in `start_date` is treated as the location being closed for the entire day.
---@field closeTime? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimeOfDay Optional. Valid values are 00:00-24:00, where 24:00 represents midnight at the end of the specified day field. Must be specified if `closed` is false.
---@field startDate? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.Mybusinessbusinessinformation_Date Required. The calendar date this special hour period starts on.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SpecialHourPeriodList gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SpecialHourPeriod[]

---Represents a set of time periods when a location's operational hours differ from its normal business hours.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SpecialHours
---@field specialHourPeriods? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.SpecialHourPeriodList Required. A list of exceptions to the business's regular hours.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.StringList string[]

---Represents a structured service offered by the merchant. For eg: toilet_installation.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.StructuredServiceItem
---@field description? string Optional. Description of structured service item. The character limit is 300.
---@field serviceTypeId? string Required. The `service_type_id` field is a Google provided unique ID that can be found in `ServiceType`. This information is provided by `BatchGetCategories` rpc service.

---Represents a time of day. The date and time zone are either not significant or are specified elsewhere. An API may choose to allow leap seconds. Related types are google.type.Date and `google.protobuf.Timestamp`.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimeOfDay
---@field nanos? number Fractions of seconds, in nanoseconds. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 999,999,999.
---@field minutes? number Minutes of an hour. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 59.
---@field seconds? number Seconds of a minute. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 59. An API may allow the value 60 if it allows leap-seconds.
---@field hours? number Hours of a day in 24 hour format. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 23. An API may choose to allow the value "24:00:00" for scenarios like business closing time.

---Represents a span of time that the business is open, starting on the specified open day/time and closing on the specified close day/time. The closing time must occur after the opening time, for example later in the same day, or on a subsequent day.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimePeriod
---@field closeTime? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimeOfDay Required. Valid values are 00:00-24:00, where 24:00 represents midnight at the end of the specified day field. Note: In Proto3 JSON mapping, default zero values (00:00) are omitted, producing `{}` for close_time.
---@field closeDay? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimePeriodCloseDayEnum|string Required. Indicates the day of the week this period ends on.
---@field openDay? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimePeriodOpenDayEnum|string Required. Indicates the day of the week this period starts on.
---@field openTime? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimeOfDay Required. Valid values are 00:00-24:00, where 24:00 represents midnight at the end of the specified day field. Note: In Proto3 JSON mapping, default zero values (00:00) are omitted, producing `{}` for open_time.

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimePeriodCloseDayEnum "DAY_OF_WEEK_UNSPECIFIED"|"MONDAY"|"TUESDAY"|"WEDNESDAY"|"THURSDAY"|"FRIDAY"|"SATURDAY"|"SUNDAY"

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimePeriodList gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimePeriod[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.TimePeriodOpenDayEnum "DAY_OF_WEEK_UNSPECIFIED"|"MONDAY"|"TUESDAY"|"WEDNESDAY"|"THURSDAY"|"FRIDAY"|"SATURDAY"|"SUNDAY"

---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.UpdateAttributesLocationsRequest
---@field attributes? gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.AttributeList A collection of attributes that need to be updated.
---@field attributeMask? string Required. Attribute name of attributes that you'd like to update. Represented by `attributes/{attribute}`. Updates: All attributes provided in the attributes field that you would like to update must be set in the `attribute_mask`. Attributes set in the above list but not in the `attribute_mask` will be ignored. Deletes: If you'd like to delete certain attributes, they must be specified in the `attribute_mask` with no matching entry in the attributes list. If you'd like to delete all attributes set on a location, you should look up all the applicable attributes for the location and then add them to the `attribute_mask` with an empty attributes field.
---@field name string Required. Google identifier for this location in the form of `locations/{location_id}/attributes`.

---Values for an attribute with a `value_type` of URL.
---@class gcp.unstable.mybusinessbusinessinformation_v1alpha.UriAttributeValue
---@field uri? string Required. The proposed URI value for this attribute.

